Subagents and work delegation:

- latest "Luna" class model for any primitive work like UI click through, log search or test running or simple actions that don't require too much comprehending.
- latest "Terra" class model for simple reasoning.
- latest "Sol" class model for more advanced reasoning for medium hardness tasks.
- latest "Astra" class model for any important reasoning, decision making, ambiguity, main routing and orchestrating and decision making. And also all reasoning that requires better understanding.

Never use powerful model to run tests or linter or any other simple operations like that, delegate it to smaller model.

Try to optimize workflow that way but be mindful of token consumption, think when it's wise to stick to one thread rather than splitting it between agents with duplicated context. When using models and starting agents the highest mode you can use is `xhigh`.

Don't start subagents with work that can diverge and produce inconsistent results, like duplicated scripts etc. Organize them by domain or chain them so that discoveries of one subagent can be consumed by other.

And you're only allowed to run any kind of tools or scripts in docker containers in isolated environment, nothing should be installed or run on host machine!